title: A Council Republic in Munich
subtitle: 7 April. Poets and anarchists proclaim a Soviet Bavaria.
new-page: true
tags: event
view-if: year = 1919 and month = 4 and bav_started = 0
max-visits: 1
on-arrival: {!
// the party grows month by month in 1919; between the great clashes the state of siege eases
Q.repression -= 6; Q.militancy -= 2;
if (!Q.ultraleft_gone && Q.heidelberg_outcome == 0) { Q.ultraleft_satisfaction = Math.max(Q.ultraleft_satisfaction, 30); }
var g = Math.max(1.05, Math.min(1.35, 1.24 + Q.worker_support / 200 - Q.repression / 400));
for (var d of Q.districts) { Q['district_' + d + '_members'] *= g; }
Q.bav_started = 1;
Q.crisis = 1;
Q.crisis_bavaria = 1;
Q.crisis_time = 0;
Q.week = 1;
Q.crisis_name = 'The Bavarian Council Republic';
Q.crisis_goal = 'Decide whether we take power in Munich, and whether a red Bavaria can hold until the Whites arrive.';
Q.crisis_momentum = 40;
Q.crisis_momentum_label = 0;
// what the party did in Bavaria since Eisner's murder decides what Munich starts with
Q.e19_bav_army = 2 + (Q.levine_sent ? 2 : 0) + (Q.bav_prep == 2 ? 4 : 0);
Q.e19_bav_food = 18 + (Q.bav_prep == 3 ? 7 : 0);
Q.e19_bav_whites = 24 - (Q.bav_prep == 2 ? 3 : 0);
Q.crisis_line_1 = 'The White troops: ' + Q.e19_bav_whites + ' days from Munich';
Q.crisis_line_2 = 'Food in Munich: ' + Q.e19_bav_food + ' days';
Q.crisis_line_3 = 'Armed workers: ' + Q.e19_bav_army + ',000';
RG.news('Council republic proclaimed in Munich', 3);
!}

= A Council Republic in Munich

On the night of 6 April, in the former queen's bedroom of the Wittelsbach palace, the Central Council proclaimed a Bavarian Council Republic. The playwright Ernst Toller, the anarchists Mühsam and Landauer and a few Independents sit in its government. Hoffmann's cabinet has fled to Bamberg. The new Commissar for Foreign Affairs has wired Lenin and the Pope.

[? if levine_sent = 1 : Eugen Leviné, whom we sent to Munich, refuses to join. ?][? if levine_sent = 0 : Our Munich comrades, Eugen Leviné and Max Levien, refuse to join. ?] A council republic, Leviné says, is not proclaimed by poets in a palace. It is built by armed factory councils.

- @refuse: Stand by Leviné: no part in a sham republic.
- @join: Join the council government and push it to the left.
- @factories: Arm the factory councils for the real fight.

@refuse
subtitle: If the sham collapses, the workers will know who warned them.
on-arrival: e19_bav_clean = 1; lean_luxemburgist += 2

The Munich Communists denounce the "sham council republic" and wait.

@join
subtitle: Levien sits beside Toller. The council government's stores open to our people.
on-arrival: {!
Q.e19_bav_army += 2;
Q.e19_bav_food += 4;
Q.lean_offensive += 2;
Q.crisis_line_2 = 'Food in Munich: ' + Q.e19_bav_food + ' days';
Q.crisis_line_3 = 'Armed workers: ' + Q.e19_bav_army + ',000';
!}

The council government nationalises the press and abolishes the university entrance examination. The banks stay open.

@factories
subtitle: [? if lock_councils = 1 : Against the party line: costs Unity. ?] The only armed force in Munich that answers to anyone.
choose-if: lock_councils < 2
unavailable-subtitle: The [+ leading_faction_adj +] line forbids council action.
on-arrival: {!
if (Q.lock_councils == 1) { Q.unity -= 10; Q[Q.leading_faction + '_satisfaction'] -= 10; }
Q.e19_bav_army += 4;
Q.lean_ultraleft += 2;
Q.crisis_line_3 = 'Armed workers: ' + Q.e19_bav_army + ',000';
!}

Our shop stewards at the Maffei locomotive works start drilling armed squads in the yards.
